@* Reusable "Design Your Own" promo card — appears after the product listing,
   but ONLY when a specific category is selected AND that category isn't
   a group's "All" view (see isGroupAllView below).

   Included by: Views/Home/hIndex.cshtml and Views/Home/hProducts.cshtml
   (both via @@await Html.PartialAsync("_CustomizeCard")).
   Reads: ViewBag.Categories / ViewBag.SelectedCategory, set by
   HomeController.hIndex() / hProducts().
   Links into: CustomizeController.Custom() for the selected category.

   Its photo is the SAME one the Customize category picker uses for that
   category (wwwroot/images/custom/{key}/ — white photo preferred, falling
   back to black, then whatever's first), so a sub-category like "Cotton
   T-Shirts" shows its own actual photo instead of a generic shared icon.

   When the shopper is on a GROUP's "All" view (e.g. browsing "T-Shirts"
   itself, not one specific sub-type like Compression), there's no single
   item to jump straight into customizing — so instead of guessing, the
   card is hidden entirely there. It still shows normally for a specific
   sub-type (Compression T-Shirts, Varsity Jackets, ...) and for
   standalone categories with no sub-types (Polo Shirts, Tote Bags,
   Sweaters). *@
@using ConceptFactory.Utils
@inject IWebHostEnvironment Environment
@{
    var categories = ViewBag.Categories as List<ConceptFactory.Models.Category>;
    int? selectedCategory = ViewBag.SelectedCategory;
    var currentCat = categories?.FirstOrDefault(c => c.CategoryID == selectedCategory);

    var promoImg = CategoryImageResolver.GetDefaultThumb(Environment, currentCat?.CategoryName, "/images/categories/default.png");

    // A "group" here means a top-level category that has sub-types under
    // it (T-Shirts, Hoodies & Jackets) — selecting it directly (or its
    // "All" subchip, which uses the same categoryId) means the shopper
    // hasn't picked a specific sub-type yet, so there's nothing specific
    // to customize — the card is hidden in that case (see below).
    bool isGroupAllView = currentCat != null && currentCat.ParentCategoryID == null
        && (categories?.Any(c => c.ParentCategoryID == currentCat.CategoryID) ?? false);
}
@if (currentCat != null && !isGroupAllView)
{
    <a asp-controller="Customize" asp-action="Custom" asp-route-categoryId="@selectedCategory"
       class="catalog-card customize-card">
        <div class="catalog-card-thumb">
            <img src="@promoImg" alt="Design Your Own @(currentCat.CategoryName)" />
            <span class="customize-card-overlay">YOUR<br>DESIGN<br>HERE</span>
        </div>
        <div class="catalog-card-body">
            <span class="catalog-card-category">Custom Order</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-name">Design Your Own</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-desc">Have your own artwork? Upload it and we'll bring it to life on any item.</span>
            <span class="catalog-card-btn">Get Started</span>
        </div>
    </a>
}
